# Apache Ranger — PR authoring rules

Goal: land a PR in `apache/ranger` with **zero avoidable review rounds**.

Two independent gates decide whether a PR merges:

1. **The build.** Checkstyle, sortpom and the enforcer plugin fail the build on violation. A red
   build is not reviewed.
2. **Committer review.** Ranger's most frequent reviewer is **Madhan Neethiraj (`mneethiraj`)**,
   who reviews the large majority of PRs. His feedback is highly consistent and almost entirely
   predictable — the recurring themes are captured in §4–§6 below, with verbatim review quotes as
   evidence.

Gate 1 is mechanical: run the build. Gate 2 is the one that costs weeks. Read §4 before writing
code, not after.

---

## 1. Pre-flight checklist

Run through this before opening (or updating) a PR:

- [ ] An ASF JIRA exists: <https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/RANGER>
- [ ] PR title starts with the JIRA id: `RANGER-XXXX: <short description>`
- [ ] **The commit message** also starts with the same JIRA id (reviewers check this separately
      from the PR title)
- [ ] PR body uses `.github/pull_request_template.md` — both sections filled in
- [ ] `mvn -T 8 clean verify` passes locally (this is exactly what CI runs)
- [ ] No binary artifacts, no `.tar.gz`, no jars, no IDE files in the diff
- [ ] Diff contains **only** what the JIRA describes — no drive-by reformatting, no unrelated renames
- [ ] Every new/changed config property follows the naming convention in §5.2
- [ ] If a DB schema changed: **all** DB flavors updated (§5.5)
- [ ] If a public/plugin-facing API changed: backward compatibility considered and stated (§4.1)

---

## 2. The build is the first reviewer

CI (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`) runs on JDK 17:

```bash
mvn -T 8 clean verify --no-transfer-progress -B -V
```

Run the same thing locally. For a fast loop on one module:

```bash
mvn -pl <module> -am -DskipTests verify
```

`verify` — not `compile`, not `install -DskipTests` — is the phase that runs Checkstyle. A build
that only "compiles" proves nothing.

### What fails the build

| Plugin | Phase | Fails on |
|---|---|---|
| `maven-checkstyle-plugin` (checkstyle 8.29) | `verify` | any violation of `dev-support/checkstyle.xml` — **including test sources** (`includeTestSourceDirectory=true`, `checkstyle.failOnViolation=true`) |
| `sortpom-maven-plugin` | `validate` | any `pom.xml` whose contents are not in sorted order (`verifyFail=Stop`, `verifyFailOn=Strict`) |
| `maven-enforcer-plugin` | `validate` | JDK < 17, Maven < 3.6.3, or a banned dependency |

If you touch any `pom.xml`, run `mvn sortpom:sort` before committing — hand-editing a pom almost
always breaks the sort check.

### Banned dependencies (enforcer, `searchTransitive=true`)

- `junit:junit` / `junit:junit-dep` at `compile`/`runtime`/`provided` — the project is on **JUnit 5**
  (`org.junit.jupiter`). Never add a JUnit 4 import to a new test.
- `com.sun.jersey:*` and `com.sun.jersey.contribs:*` — the project is on **Jersey 2.x**
  (`org.glassfish.jersey.*`). Only `test`-scoped Jersey 1 is tolerated, for Hadoop mini-cluster
  test infrastructure.

`spotbugs.failOnViolation` is `false`, so SpotBugs warnings do not break the build — but they are
still visible to reviewers.

---

## 3. Checkstyle rules, stated plainly

The authoritative files are `dev-support/checkstyle.xml` and
`dev-support/checkstyle-suppressions.xml`. Read them before a large refactor. The rules that bite
most often:

### Whitespace and file hygiene

- **No tabs**, ever. 4-space indent. Continuation/line-wrap indent is **8** spaces
  (`lineWrappingIndentation=8`, `throwsIndent=8`).
- **LF** line endings; a carriage return anywhere is a violation.
- Exactly one newline at end of file; no blank line immediately before EOF.
- No trailing whitespace; no whitespace before a closing `)`.
- No **two or more consecutive blank lines**.
- No blank line immediately after `{`, and none immediately before `}`.
- Lambda: opening brace on the same line as `->`; no whitespace inside an empty lambda body.
- `new Type[] {` — exactly one space before the array initializer brace, never zero and never two.

### Imports

`ImportOrder` is configured as `groups="*,javax,java"`, `separated=true`, `option="bottom"`,
alphabetically sorted. So every Java file looks like:

```java
package org.apache.ranger.plugin.policyengine;

import org.apache.commons.collections.CollectionUtils;
import org.apache.commons.lang3.StringUtils;
import org.apache.ranger.plugin.model.RangerPolicy;
import org.slf4j.Logger;
import org.slf4j.LoggerFactory;

import javax.servlet.http.HttpServletRequest;

import java.util.List;
import java.util.Map;

import static org.apache.ranger.plugin.policyengine.PolicyEvaluatorForTag.MATCH_TYPE_COMPARATOR;
```

- Everything else first (alphabetical), then `javax`, then `java`, then **static imports last**,
  blank line between each group.
- **No star imports.** No unused imports. No redundant imports.

### Static-import rules (the surprising ones)

Must **not** be statically imported:

- `X.of`, `X.copyOf`, `X.valueOf`, `X.builder`
- anything `.format` other than `java.lang.String.format`
- any member of `java.util.Optional`

Must **only** be used **via** static import (i.e. write `requireNonNull(x)`, never
`Objects.requireNonNull(x)`):

- `Objects.requireNonNull`
- `Math.toIntExact`
- `ImmutableMap.toImmutableMap`, `ImmutableList.toImmutableList`, `ImmutableSet.toImmutableSet`
- `org.testng.Assert`
- `com.google.common.base.MoreObjects`, `Preconditions`, `Verify`

### Structure

- `NeedBraces` — every `if`/`for`/`while`/`do` gets braces, even one-liners.
- `LeftCurly` at end of line; closing brace of an `else` block alone on its line.
- `OneStatementPerLine`, `MultipleVariableDeclarations` — one declaration, one statement per line.
- `EmptyLineSeparator` — blank line between methods, constructors, class defs and import blocks
  (consecutive fields may be packed).
- `ExplicitInitialization` — do **not** write `private String name = null;` or `int count = 0;`.
- `StringLiteralEquality` — never compare strings with `==`.
- `EqualsHashCode` — override both or neither.
- `InnerAssignment` — no assignment inside an expression.
- `HideUtilityClassConstructor` — a class with only static members needs a private constructor.
- `OneTopLevelClass`, `PackageDeclaration`, `ArrayTypeStyle` (`String[] x`, not `String x[]`).
- `IllegalToken: LITERAL_ASSERT` — **`assert` is banned** in all sources, tests included. Use a
  JUnit 5 assertion.
- `DefaultComesLast`, `ModifierOrder`, `UpperEll` (`1L`, not `1l`), `RedundantModifier`
  (no `public` on interface methods).

### Naming

`MemberName`, `LocalVariableName`, `LocalFinalVariableName`, `ParameterName`, `StaticVariableName`
all require `camelCase` (no underscores, no leading `m`/`s` prefixes). `TypeName` requires
`PascalCase`. Package names are lowercase-only.

Do **not** add new entries to `checkstyle-suppressions.xml`. The existing entries are legacy
(mostly `TypeName` for `PatchXxx_J100nn` DB-patch classes); new code is expected to comply.

