## 4. What `mneethiraj` actually asks for

These are the recurring review themes, each backed by a verbatim comment from a real PR. If your
patch trips one of these, expect a review round.

### 4.1 Backward compatibility is the first question asked

Any change to a public model, a service-def, an audit field, a REST payload or a plugin-facing API
gets checked against existing deployments.

> "wouldn't swapping setAccessType() and setAction() implementation result in backward
> compatibility issue in audit logs being generated by all plugins that exist currently?" — PR #243

> "this fix will not address Ranger deployments that already have earlier Trino service-def. In
> addition to this fix in Trino service-def, I suggest UI updates to not duplicate configurations
> included in the service-def." — PR #1170

> "Given many existing plugins require JDK8 support, it is critical to be able to build with
> earlier version JDK as well." — PR #291

**Rule:** when you change a service-def, a stored JSON shape, or a DB row, say in the PR
description what happens to *already-upgraded* installs, and add the DB patch / upgrade path — or
explain why none is needed (e.g. *"this service-def is still in DRAFT mode"*, PR #888).

### 4.2 Reuse what exists before adding something new

Adding a parallel API, a parallel property, or a parallel code path is the single most common
reason a PR gets sent back.

> "GdsREST already has following API to bulk-delete shared resources... Perhaps adding an API to
> bulk-update is good enough? i.e. is an API to update or delete necessary?" — PR #932

> "Consider using existing property `fasterxml.jackson.version` (line # 215) instead of introducing
> new one `com.fasterxml.jackson.version`." — PR #252

> "How is `ACCESS_TYPE_SERVICE_NOTIFICATION_POST` different from `ACCESS_TYPE_POST_NOTIFICATION`?
> If they are not different, I suggest removing `ACCESS_TYPE_SERVICE_NOTIFICATION_POST`." — PR #1219

> "with this approach (of having `isAccessAllowedSync()` methods), every plugin must be updated to
> call `*Sync()` method version instead of existing calls to `isAccessAllowed()`... I suggest
> avoiding updates to large number of modules, and go with the approach in this PR." — PR #595

**Rule:** before adding a constant, property, REST endpoint or method overload, grep for an
existing one. A change that forces every plugin to be updated will be rejected in favour of one
that doesn't.

### 4.3 Don't add API surface speculatively

> "Is it necessary to expose this method via REST, given `id` is an internal field (i.e, generated
> by Ranger/DB)?" ... "I suggest to introduce this API when we add UI for this." — PR #683

> "Consider marking `processMessageBatch()` as `private` as it is called only from this class."
> — PR #886

**Rule:** narrowest visibility that works. No REST API without a caller. No `public` method that
only this class calls.

### 4.4 Names must state intent

Renames are requested constantly, and they are not optional nits.

> "I suggest renaming method `checkAccountNotDisabled()` to `ensureUserIsActive()`. Also, update
> the messages to replace 'disabled' with 'not active'." — PR #1174

> "`keysToRemove` ==> `permissionsToRemove`" — PR #988

> "`downloadUserGroupsEnabled` => `includeUserGroupMappings`" — PR #1185

> "Consider renaming SERVICE_NOT_FOUND => NOT_FOUND." — PR #110

> "The API is called `UPDATE_SHARED_RESOURCES`, but the flag is named a `forceDelete`. It will help
> to add a note on the purpose of this API." — PR #932

> "userLoginId paramter name is misleading. The value sent is the name provided in the view object
> ... This name should not be trusted." — PR #788

**Rule:** the identifier must describe *what it is*, not *how it got here* or *what triggered it*;
and the name of a flag must match the name of the API it belongs to.

### 4.5 Do the fix once, at the right layer

> "how about adding `normalize()` method in `RangerServiceDef` which will perform the operation in
> thread-safe way. This will isolate the details within `RangerServiceDef`." — PR #1112

> "instead of taking this fix and then subsequent patch to move normalization to RangerServiceDef,
> why not skip the current fix and directly go with the final/desired fix?" — PR #1112

**Rule:** put the logic inside the class that owns the data. Don't land a stop-gap with a promise
to refactor later — go straight to the intended design.

### 4.6 Keep the diff minimal

> "thank you for the PR. I suggest to keep the fix simpler - by keeping only changes in
> `dev-support/ranger-docker/scripts/admin/create-ranger-services.py`." — PR #1212

> "the comments have become too noisy, hence my suggestion to keeps the code simple for humans to
> read. I would suggest only the following 2 changes..." — PR #1143

> "I suggest replacing this file (`log_config.py`) with addition of following line at the begining
> of `create_ranger_services.py`: `logging.basicConfig(...)`" — PR #920

**Rule:** a new file, a new abstraction or a new helper must earn its place. Solve it inline if
inline is readable.

### 4.7 Remove redundant work and redundant checks

> "`hivePlugin` will not null here given the caller already references it at line 2847. I suggest
> removing the `if` at 2884." — PR #988

> "Initialize the header name in `init()` method, instead of reading from config on every call."
> — PR #873

> "Given this script is executed in the container running ranger admin service, it seem call to
> `socket.gethostname()` is not necessary; simply using `localhost` would work, right?" — PR #922

**Rule:** read configuration once at init. Don't null-check a reference the caller already
dereferenced. Don't recompute per-request what is constant per-process.

### 4.8 Correctness of authorization logic gets read line by line

> "when scope is null, shouldn't the return be true if matchType is SELF or
> SELF_AND_ALL_DESCENDANTS?" — PR #410

> "case blocks for `SELF_OR_DESCENDANTS` and `SELF_AND_ALL_DESCENDANTS` are the same, which doesn't
> look correct. Can you review?" — PR #410

> "if multiple policies grant this permission to the principal, removing the permission based on
> just one policy (line 2904) will result in incorrect ACLs." — PR #988

> "Shouldn't admin users be allowed as well? `boolean ret = bizUtil.isAdmin() ||
> bizUtil.isAuditAdmin();`" — PR #1214

> "this could result in usernames having valid non-English characters (accent characters, CJK
> character sets) to be skipped with default configuration. This can break environments already
> have such user names and group names." — PR #903

**Rule:** enumerate every enum/`matchType`/null case explicitly, and check that the
admin/super-user branch is consistent with the equivalent code elsewhere in the module. Never
restrict identifiers to ASCII by default.

### 4.9 Packaging and dependencies are part of the change

Removing a library from code is only half the job.

> "With this patch, commons-lang library is no more needed, hence can be removed from packaging as
> well - in files under `distro/src/main/assembly`. Can you please review and update?" — PR #724

> "can you please verify that the final packaging does not include codehaus jackson library?"
> — PR #252

> "with inclusion of audit server destination in plugins packaging, I suggest removing other
> destinations from packaging (hdfs, solr). This will eliminate many dependent libraries from
> plugins" — PR #969

**Rule:** if you drop a dependency, drop it from `distro/src/main/assembly/*.xml` too, and verify
the built tarball. If you add one, justify it.

