## 5. Ranger-specific conventions

### 5.1 Java code style (what the codebase actually looks like)

Reference file for a new model class: `authz-api/src/main/java/org/apache/ranger/authz/model/RangerAuthzRequest.java`.
Reference for engine-style code: `agents-common/src/main/java/org/apache/ranger/plugin/policyengine/RangerPolicyEngineImpl.java`.

**Vertical alignment.** Consecutive field declarations, and consecutive assignments, are aligned.
This is not decoration — it is the house style (`ALIGN_GROUP_FIELD_DECLARATIONS`,
`ALIGN_CONSECUTIVE_ASSIGNMENTS` in `dev-support/RangerCodeScheme-IntelliJ.xml`) and unaligned code
reads as foreign:

```java
private final PolicyEngine                 policyEngine;
private final RangerAccessRequestProcessor requestProcessor;
private final ServiceConfig                serviceConfig;

public RangerPolicyEngineImpl(...) {
    policyEngine     = new PolicyEngine(servicePolicies, pluginContext, roles, isUseReadWriteLock);
    serviceConfig    = new ServiceConfig(servicePolicies.getServiceConfig());
    requestProcessor = new RangerDefaultRequestProcessor(policyEngine);
}
```

Align only within a consecutive block; do not pad unrelated lines.

**Single `ret`, single return.** The dominant idiom in production code is one result variable named
`ret`, assigned in branches and returned once at the end (~560 `return ret;` sites in
`agents-common` alone). Prefer it for new and edited methods:

```java
public static RangerPolicyEngine getPolicyEngine(final RangerPolicyEngineImpl other, final ServicePolicies servicePolicies) {
    RangerPolicyEngine ret = null;

    if (other != null && servicePolicies != null) {
        PolicyEngine policyEngine = other.policyEngine.cloneWithDelta(servicePolicies);

        if (policyEngine != null) {
            ret = (policyEngine == other.policyEngine) ? other : new RangerPolicyEngineImpl(policyEngine, other);
        }
    }

    return ret;
}
```

Short guard clauses do exist in the codebase (notably in `equals()`), so this is a strong
preference rather than an absolute ban — but a method that returns from five places will be asked
to use `ret`.

**Braces.** `} else {`, `} catch (...) {`, `} finally {` all stay on one line with the closing
brace.

**Logging.** slf4j with `{}` placeholders — never string concatenation, and no
`if (LOG.isDebugEnabled())` wrapper around a parameterized call:

```java
LOG.debug("==> RangerAdminRESTClient.getRolesIfUpdated({}, {})", lastKnownRoleVersion, lastActivationTimeInMillis);
...
LOG.debug("<== RangerAdminRESTClient.getRolesIfUpdated({}, {}): {}", lastKnownRoleVersion, lastActivationTimeInMillis, ret);
```

The `==>` / `<==` method entry/exit convention is used throughout (400+ sites in `agents-common`);
follow it in the class you are editing. Reviewers also ask for an `info` log at the point a change
takes effect:

> "Add a info level log here: `LOG.info(\"Deleted {} pluginInfo records, for criteria={}\", ...)`" — PR #683

**Model classes.** Jackson annotations, aligned fields, telescoping constructors delegating via
`this(...)`, `Objects.hash` / `Objects.equals`, `toString()` built by concatenation or a
`StringBuilder toString(StringBuilder sb)` pair — see `RangerAuthzRequest`.

**Blank lines** are used deliberately: one blank line after a variable-declaration block, around
`if`/`try` blocks, and before `return`. Dense, unbroken method bodies read as foreign here too.

### 5.2 Configuration property naming

Plugin-side properties follow `ranger.plugin.<serviceType>.<area>.<setting>`; admin-side follow
`ranger.admin.<area>.<setting>`. The setting name states the behaviour, and boolean settings read
as predicates.

> "to be consistent with rest of policy related plugin configurations, I suggest using property
> prefix `ranger.plugin.<serviceType>.policy.` I suggest renaming `cache.refresh.mode` to
> `refresh.synchronous`, with default value as `false` — `ranger.plugin.hive.policy.refresh.synchronous`.
> `isSynchronousPolicyCacheUpdateEnabled()` => `isSynchronousPolicyRefresh()`" — PR #595

> "This configuration is used in the plugin side (and not in Ranger admin server). Hence, I suggest
> using existing convention in naming configurations - `\"ranger.plugin.\" + serviceType + \".policy.refresh.synchronous\"`." — PR #595

> "I suggest renaming the property to `ranger.admin.userstore.include.usergroups.mappings`." — PR #1185

**Rule:** name the property by *where it is read* (plugin vs admin), keep the accessor name and the
property name in sync, and make the default `false` for a new opt-in flag.

### 5.3 REST API conventions

- `{id}` vs `{name}` are separate endpoints, not overloads of one path:
  > "to be consistent with use of `{id}` and `{name}` in APIs, I would suggest to retain `{id}` in
  > this API and introduce another API for using `{name}` - like:
  > `/api/roles/name/{name}/addUserAndGroups`." — PR #135
- Prefer query params over a request body for a list of ids on `DELETE`:
  > "would marking `resourceIds` parameter as `@QueryParam(\"id\")` help to receive the IDs as query
  > params instead of body?" — PR #932
- Guard every endpoint with `@PreAuthorize("@rangerPreAuthSecurityHandler.isAPIAccessible(...)")`
  and make the admin/super-user check consistent with sibling endpoints (§4.8).
- Never derive an identity used for authorization from a caller-supplied field in the view object
  (§4.4, PR #788).

### 5.4 Tests

- **JUnit 5 only** (`org.junit.jupiter`). JUnit 4 is banned by the enforcer.
- `assert` is banned by Checkstyle — use `Assertions.assertEquals` etc.
- Test sources are checkstyle-checked; the same formatting rules apply.
- Python: tests live in `intg/src/test/python/test_ranger_client.py`, one `TestCase` per client area.

### 5.5 Database changes

> "Database scripts for other flavors (example: MySQL, Oracle) should be updated as well." — PR #1120

A schema change means **all** of `security-admin/db/{mysql,postgres,oracle,sqlanywhere,sqlserver}`
plus the corresponding `PatchXxx_J100nn` Java patch class. Updating only Postgres is an automatic
review round. (Note `sqlserver` is being retired — check current master before adding to it:
*"`sqlserver` is no more supported."* — PR #1057.)

Also ask whether a DB patch is needed at all:

> "Are changes in `PatchForOzoneServiceDefPolicyConditionUpdate_J10065.java` necessary, given
> `RangerServiceDefService.java` handles service-def updates based on feature-flag ... If no
> additional cases are handled here, I suggest reverting" — PR #1073

### 5.6 Docker / dev-support

- Container-specific scripts and configs go in container-specific directories (RANGER-4898).
- Prefer shipping one config file per flavour and copying the right one at container init over
  programmatically rewriting XML at runtime (PR #920).
- Don't download large artifacts on every build (PR #302).
- Don't start services a compose file doesn't need (PR #1057).

