## 6. Anti-patterns — reject these in your own diff

| # | Anti-pattern | Why it gets flagged |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Binary files, tarballs, jars in the PR | PR #291 — "Can you please remove this file and update the PR?" |
| 2 | Unrelated reformatting mixed into a functional change | Hides the real diff; reviewers ask for it to be split |
| 3 | New constant/property/API that duplicates an existing one | §4.2 |
| 4 | `*Sync()` / `*V2()` / `*Ex()` parallel method variants | §4.2, PR #595 |
| 5 | A REST endpoint with no caller or UI | §4.3, PR #683 |
| 6 | `public` where `private` would do | PR #886 |
| 7 | Reading config inside a per-request method | PR #873 |
| 8 | Null-checking a reference the caller already dereferenced | PR #988 |
| 9 | Names that describe the trigger rather than the value (`downloadUserGroupsEnabled`) | §4.4 |
| 10 | Flag name that contradicts its API name (`UPDATE_...` + `forceDelete`) | PR #932 |
| 11 | Service-def / model change with no upgrade path for existing installs | §4.1 |
| 12 | Schema change in one DB flavor only | §5.5 |
| 13 | Dropping a library from code but leaving it in `distro/src/main/assembly` | §4.9 |
| 14 | Stop-gap fix with "will refactor in a follow-up JIRA" | §4.5, PR #1112 |
| 15 | New helper file/class for something that is one line inline | §4.6, PR #920 |
| 16 | Verbose commented-out alternatives left in scripts | PR #1143 — "the comments have become too noisy" |
| 17 | String concatenation in a log call, or `isDebugEnabled()` around a parameterized call | §5.1 |
| 18 | `assert` in tests, or a JUnit 4 import | §3, §5.4 |
| 19 | Star imports, unsorted imports, static import of `of`/`valueOf`/`builder` | §3 |
| 20 | `private String x = null;` / `private int n = 0;` | `ExplicitInitialization` |
| 21 | Hand-edited `pom.xml` (breaks sortpom) | §2 |
| 22 | Tabs, CRLF, trailing whitespace, double blank lines | §3 |
| 23 | Restricting usernames/groups to ASCII | PR #903 |
| 24 | Trusting a caller-supplied name for an authorization decision | PR #788 |
| 25 | Wrong/missing JIRA id in the **commit message** (even when the PR title is right) | Flagged on PR #1185 |

