## 7. Responding to review

- Address **every** comment — either with a code change or with a reply explaining why not.
  Silent force-pushes over open threads stall a PR.
- When a reviewer proposes a concrete alternative (often as a code block, sometimes as an attached
  `.patch`), take it or explain precisely why it doesn't work. The suggestions are usually the
  final shape the committer intends to merge.
- Push fixes as new commits during review; don't rewrite history mid-review.
- "This is a nit" is not a category that exists here — rename requests are expected to be applied.
- Re-run `mvn -T 8 clean verify` after every review round. A style fix that breaks Checkstyle costs
  another full cycle.

---

## 8. Quick reference

```bash
# what CI runs
mvn -T 8 clean verify --no-transfer-progress -B -V

# fast single-module check (includes checkstyle)
mvn -pl <module> -am -DskipTests verify

# after touching any pom.xml
mvn sortpom:sort

# checkstyle config
dev-support/checkstyle.xml
dev-support/checkstyle-suppressions.xml
dev-support/RangerCodeScheme-IntelliJ.xml   # import into IntelliJ
```

Related rules: `.cursor/rules/ranger-checkstyle.mdc` (checkstyle detail),
`.cursor/rules/ranger-python.mdc` (Python client conventions).
